Z||000000||Loki||02-28-2001||12:38 PM||||Temp light is coming on only under had acceleration but not fully on, just flickers and will go away once im off the gas...Any clue as to why it would do this? I cant tell yet if its over heating (which i know its not) since it has no coolant temp sensor but this is new..could it be the car is not used to the -5 nights yet?<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki137/loki5.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||02-28-2001||07:02 PM||||probably pinching the wire someplace. you need to find where before it pinches something important. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GTZ34||03-01-2001||05:37 PM||||This is going to sound wierd but...  How are your motor mounts and strut brace?  If your engine is moving excessively (under hard accelleration) it might be pulling wires or something like Ogre said, probably shorting somewhere.||||reg||1
Z||000003||862M4inCA||03-01-2001||08:40 PM||||Ok now, someone correct me if I am wrong, but isn't the temperature sensor for BOTH the light AND the gauge? I know on my 2.5 it's located at the upper left hand side of the head and has two wires connect that when unplugged the gauge goes dead, and when I ground the wires (both or individually) either the light comes on, or the gauge pegs. Just seems very suspicious that it's a wire being pinched, or short somewhere.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Loki||03-01-2001||10:03 PM||||Acctually after diging around in the engine compartment..the two wires that plug into the coolant sensor are loose.....Could that be a cause? Im sure it is but was just asking...<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki137/loki5.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
